# Star-Mural — one pattern, four bricks, one baseplate.
#
# The other presets here each print one piece. This one prints a *set*: a
# 3 × 3 field of {8/3} stars is cut along the stud grid into 2 × 2 pieces of
# 4 × 4 studs each, and the pieces reconstitute the field when placed
# adjacently on a store-bought baseplate. The centre star is quartered by
# both cut lines and the edge stars are halved by one — deliberately, so
# every seam runs through art and the set demonstrates the thing a mural
# exists to demonstrate: fragments cut from one planar graph carry the same
# vertices on both sides of every seam, so the pattern continues across
# pieces to within the 0.2 mm physical part gap.
#
# The art is cut at the *nominal* 8 mm grid lines; the body's `8n − 0.2`
# footprint then clips 0.1 mm per side, which is what the seam interrupts.
# Nothing here re-registers the art to the gap — the gap is physical, the
# cut is nominal, and conflating the two is the K10 defect the design doc
# (3d-models `docs/lego-pattern-set-design.md` §3) exists to name.
#
# Expect a V12 bridge warning per piece, and it is the set's honest price:
# an anchor may not sit within its ribbed reach of a pocket edge, and a
# 12 mm star parked over a 4 × 4 piece's centre rejects the five anchors
# under and beside it (§5.2 droppedForRelief), leaving the four corner
# tubes and a ~16 mm bridged ceiling run — over the 10 mm CAL-BRG-01
# default, which is a slicer setting, not a measured span. Art this large
# trades interior clutch for pattern; that trade is the point of the demo.
#
# Render:
#   bikar render patterns/Lego/Star-Mural.bkr --format parts --check -o star-mural/
#     (one STL per piece, StarMural-P_c0r0.stl … + the layout report)
#   bikar render patterns/Lego/Star-Mural.bkr --format ldraw -o StarMural.mpd
#     (one MPD, geometry-keyed FILE blocks — a digital pre-assembly)
#   bikar render patterns/Lego/Star-Mural.bkr --format svg -o StarMural.svg
#     (the whole field, uncut — the art check before plastic)
#
# Every dimension the clutch depends on is an unmeasured bet (CAL-RIB-01,
# coupon LG-F1), and seam registration on a real plate is its own bet
# (CAL-REG-01, coupon LG-P1). Print the coupons before trusting the fit.

param plates = 3 range 2..9 step 1
param relief = 0.8 range 0.8..2.0 step 0.1

blueprint star_cell
  circle G center(0,0) radius 8
  divide G into 4 offset 0
  circle S center(0,0) radius 6
  divide S into 8 offset 0

pattern star_motif on star_cell
  connect every 3 on S

pattern star_field
  tile star_motif
    repeat_x 3
    repeat_y 3
    offset_col G.cpt2 G.cpt0
    offset_row G.cpt3 G.cpt1
    mode rectangular
  voids detect

mural StarMural
  inscribe star_field
  pieces 2 x 2 of 4 x 4
  height $plates plates
  relief depth $relief
